{"id":151928760441083,"type":"album","name":"Replica","artist":"Oneohtrix Point Never","year":2011,"weight":22,"info":{"cover":"https://cdn2.albumoftheyear.org/600x0/album/2942-replica_171233.jpg","aoty":79,"aoty_user":84,"sputnik":3.97,"yt":"YXvMft3nXGQ","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/oneohtrix-point-never/replica","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/2942-oneohtrix-point-never-replica.php","sputnikmusic":"https://www.sputnikmusic.com/album/85787/Oneohtrix-Point-Never-Replica/"},"desc":"\"Replica\" is an electronic song cycle based around audio procured from TV ad compilations. These sample-based meditations are as lyrical as they are ecological, featuring re-purposed “ghost vocals” which serve as narration for Lopatin’s signature amorphous, ambient passages. Lopatin’s Juno-60 is still prominent, but \"Returnal\"’s placid, synthetic surroundings are accelerated through darker, more unpredictable terrains via Lopatin’s use of samplers, analog filtering, tape-op, piano, plate reverb and sub-bass. The result is a heightened sense of music as part and parcel of an overall sonic terrain. ."},"artist_ref":{"id":107299411439580,"name":"Oneohtrix Point Never","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/ONEOHTRIX_POINT_NEVER_%28cropped%29.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":68317475436284,"type":"genre","name":"Vaporwave","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":337,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":137823799025216,"type":"genre","name":"Glitch","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":247,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":159918588106246,"type":"genre","name":"Progressive Electronic","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":226,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":79811058028299,"type":"genre","name":"Plunderphonics","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":221,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"},{"id":11539588044819,"type":"genre","name":"Broken Transmission","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":216,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"i